Canis latrans", "Urocyon cinereoargenteus"], "bear>coyote": ["ga", "Canis latrans", "Ursus americanus"]}, "story": "Big Bend National Park in West Texas protects the largest area of Chihuahuan Desert in the United States. It holds more than 1,200 plant species, 450 bird species, 56 reptiles and 75 mammals. The Chisos Mountains lie wholly inside the park, and the Chisos oak grows nowhere else in the country.", "matters": "Isolated plants and animals in the Chisos Mountains and desert springs make up much of its biodiversity. The Rio Grande's riparian zone is highly productive."}